    songTitle: "SEELE BRENNT (Soul On Fire)",
    bioGreeting: "“Seele brennt” (“Soul on Fire”) is a song about the invisible battles we sometimes fight within ourselves. It describes the feeling of being trapped in dark rooms of memories, fear and old wounds, desperately searching for a way out while no one else can see what is happening inside.\n\nThe song moves between loneliness, vulnerability and the hope of finally breaking free. Its recurring images of shadows, scars, coldness and a burning soul turn emotional pain into something almost physical.\n\nAt first, the story is deeply personal: “My soul is burning, but no one sees me.” But towards the end, the perspective changes from “me” to “you”. What began as one person’s inner struggle suddenly reaches out to someone else — a reminder that behind the face we see, another person may be fighting the very same battle.\n\n\nAbout the Team:\n\nStefan Engel and Stefan Silva first met through their work as flight attendants and soon discovered that they shared another passion: music and the Eurovision Song Contest.\n\nStefan Silva (LOURO) sings in a choir and, like Stefan Engel, has been a devoted Eurovision fan for many years. With his Portuguese roots, he also has a special connection to Portugal and follows the Portuguese national selection with particular interest.\n\n“Seele brennt” brings together three people and their different musical perspectives. The lyrics were written by Stefan Engel, while the music was composed by Stefan Lauro and Marcus Seiler.\n\nWhat started as a friendship through aviation and a shared enthusiasm for Eurovision has now turned into a musical collaboration — and “Seele brennt” is the result.\n",
