    bioGreeting: "Greetings from London! My name is Andy Brook. I’ve been lucky enough to win this competition twice in the past - most recently in 2020. It is a highlight of the musical year to be involved in this contest, whether as performer or host, and I’d like to take this opportunity to wish all the contestants the very best of luck.\nThis year my entry is called “Storia d’amore con la vita” and it is performed in Italian, with lyrics specially adapted from the original English version by Italian singer-songwriter Adriana Spuria.\nI am joined on the recording by Sharon Crawford, a classically-trained Canadian soprano, who has Icelandic roots, and who now lives in London, UK.\nGuitar and bass is played by Alex Bonnano and drums by Paolo Conte, both from Italy.\nSharon Crawford is very excited that her native Canada is joining the Eurovision Song Contest, and we are delighted to represent Canada for its debut in the Home Composed Song Contest.\nThe English version of our entry is called “Sky kisses earth”\u00a0 and I got the inspiration for the song from the name of a local shop which sold mystic items. It is a love song about life, and a love of the sky, the earth and the natural wonders that surround us. The Italian lyrics are freely adapted from the English, and I hope that native Italians won’t be too put off by my English accent!\n\nYou can watch and listen to the English version of my song on my youtube channel, AndyBrookMusic, but for the Home Composed Song Contest I am delighted to present to you the Italian version: “Storia d’amore con la vita” ,\u00a0 together with my Canadian and Italian co-musicians.",
